  k = 0.05 at z = 3 with xi = 403, P_fw/P_obs: PERMODE: 0.316, CUM-EFE: 0.64, RMS-EFE: 0.0037  (per-mode lands inside the 2x window at xi = 329-403; the others overshoot the cut)
  [PASS] B3 sign control: the literal reading chi = W ln N fed to the kernel INCREASES the k = 0.05 growth (deeper MOND at large scales); the action must filter the enhancement, not the kernel's input   (k=0.05 power ratio (KERNEL xi=403 / no filter) = 164.71)
  the small-scale side, k = 1-10 at z = 3 (the filter is transparent there): PERMODE 1.56e+03, 9.52e+03, 6e+04 ; CUM-EFE 8.1e-15, 3.73e-14, 3.22e-14 ; RMS-EFE 1.33e-14, 6.17e-14, 5.32e-14
